      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>Used to set the flag in the bitmask passed to the callback of onReceiveTextSms(MessagePdu, String, int, int, ResultCallback) to indicate that a new message notification should not be shown to the user when the credential-encrypted storage of the device is not available before the user unlocks the phone. It is only applicable to devices that support file-based encryption.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/service/carrier/CarrierMessagingService#RECEIVE_OPTIONS_SKIP_NOTIFY_WHEN_CREDENTIAL_PROTECTED_STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.service.carrier.CarrierMessagingService.RECEIVE_OPTIONS_SKIP_NOTIFY_WHEN_CREDENTIAL_PROTECTED_STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE</code>.</a></format></para>
